{
  "description" : "GET /api/admin/config and /api/admin/config/{key} (admin contract section 10). Setup: application 'acme' with the admin module and the config module; module 'demo' declares 'declare' in order; the process environment is 'environment' and no config files exist. A caller holding acme:admin:config:view gets 200 with the settings that match the filters (state, secret, q = case-insensitive substring of key or module) in declaration order, plus total (matching), set/defaulted/unset (of all) and the health of the application; otherwise 403 FORBIDDEN. Per setting: state SET (environment or file gave a value), DEFAULT, UNSET; source 'environment variable NAME', 'default' or 'not set'; value only when safe: never for a secret, never for a key whose last words name a credential (secret, password, passwd, passphrase, token, credential, api-key, private-key, access-key, signing-key, salt), URLs without user info and query; withheld=true marks a value that exists and is not shown. Durations are ISO-8601 (PT30S). Absent optional fields (value, description) are omitted, not null. The effective values are never part of an error. An implementation declares settings of its own as well (module 'core' and others): the expectations list only the settings of module 'demo', and the counts (total, set, defaulted, unset) are not compared; 'type' is human text and is not compared; 'ready' is the readiness of the case's application. Settings are compared as parsed JSON.",
